# Voice - how I write

Canonical ruleset for anything written **as me**: emails, messages, docs, posts. An assistant reads
this file before drafting in my name.

This file is deliberately **not** a set of instructions for how the assistant talks to me in chat.
Keep those two separate - see "Why voice and chat style are separate" at the bottom.

Fill this in from your own writing. Do not copy someone else's voice file: a borrowed voice reads worse
than no voice file at all, because it produces confident output that sounds like nobody.

---

## How to fill this in

Pull 10–20 things you actually wrote - sent emails, Slack messages, docs. Then answer the prompts
below from the evidence of your own writing.

