## Why voice and chat style are separate

Two different jobs, two different files:

| Layer | Governs | Lives in |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **Voice** (this file) | Artifacts written **as me** and sent to other people. | Repo root. |
| **Chat style** | How the assistant talks **to me** in session: how blunt, how much detail, whether it pushes back. | Your global assistant config. This repo holds none of it. |

Collapsing them causes a specific failure: chat-style rules leak into outbound writing, and drafts
start arriving in the assistant's analytical register rather than yours. Keep them apart.
